{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EditingHolds","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every other exemption is inferred: ","type":"text"},{"code":"Swidux\/EntityStore\/changes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writer’s drained-but-unflushed buffers, and the failed-flush ledger all","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"describe writes the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"store"}]},{"type":"text","text":" has seen. A value still sitting in a view’s local"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" is in none of them, so under"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/preferRemote","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" a remote edit can land underneath a half-typed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"field and the user’s next keystroke dispatches against a value that changed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out from under them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A hold closes exactly that window, and nothing wider:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["TextEditor(text: $draft)","    .holdsEntity(note.id, in: persistence.editing)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Prefer that modifier — it takes the hold when the editor appears and gives it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"back when the editor goes away, so there is no release to forget. Reach for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/hold(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/release(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" directly only where the editing session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"isn’t a view’s lifetime."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"What a hold is not","anchor":"What-a-hold-is-not","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A hold "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"defers a remote change; it does not veto one."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Release it and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"next merge applies whatever storage holds, including a deletion made"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elsewhere. The worst a leaked hold can do is strand one row at a stale"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value, which is what "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/preferInMemory"},{"type":"text","text":" does on purpose. It is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not data loss, and it is not silent either: a merge that actually withheld a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"differing value reports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/PersistenceDiagnostic\/mergeWithheld(entityType:ids:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two alternatives cost less and are often enough. ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.binding(_:sending:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dispatches on write, which makes the value a drained-but-unflushed one and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers it already. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/MergePolicy\/preferInMemory","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" exempts a whole collection","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"permanently. A hold sits between them: remote-wins stays on everywhere else,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and here only while the user is actually typing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"IDs an app has declared it is editing, exempt from a re-hydration merge for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as long as the hold is in force."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/editingholds"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence"]]},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/init()"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/ids","doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EditingHolds\/isEmpty"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/Editing